           (or intentional multi-target where a single source spans >1 target). 30 target paragraphs
           total (up from the original 15). Q4 (utrum viator operibus meritoriis insistendo ex hiis
           carior deo fiat). Extremely compressed relative to other questions.

           MULTI-TARGET single sources (one src spans >1 target, interleaving): d613->d202,d244
           (dicendum quod propositio proposita vera est / ad argumentum in contrarium conceditur);
           d2256->d367 only (its earlier portion, matched by a duplicate/adjacent id in the sorb193
           pass, went to d355/d295); d2306->d395,d427 (probatur videtur... / respondent nostri doctores).

           d284 (2nd-dubium resolution "Respondetur concedendo propositum et ad argumenta respondetur
           vtrobique negando consequentiam") aligned with d893 rather than d838: d893 ("primum
           argumentum probat verum propositum et rationes in oppositum ostendunt non oppositum illius
           sed istius") mirrors the same concede-the-proposition/deny-the-consequence structure
           applied to the same d715/d803/d820 argument set; d838 is a self-contained technical
           argument with no structural echo, so it was dropped.

           MASSIVE DROP: dubia 3, 4, and 5 in their entirety (sources d904 through d1981, ~31
           paragraphs) are compressed away with no target parallel; Oyta skips straight from the
           2nd-dubium response to the principal-argument response (d1997, relocated to d290). Also
           dropped: d346, d384 (proportio sub-arguments in dubium 1), d838 (dubium-2 resolution
           detail, see d284/d893 note above), d2191, d2233, d2243, d2352 (minor citations/args in
           the coste-multiplication section), d174 (ex hiis potest argui, no match), and d2497
           (final synthesis paragraph, no target text found; flag for review, unusual to drop the
           concluding paragraph).

           FULLY SPLIT to 1:1; all 30 targets referenced exactly once, no dangling refs. -->
